{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:8dccb6eaa7710597","name":"T-65XJ3 X-Wing Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-8dccb6eaa7710597","title":"T-65XJ3 X-Wing Starfighter","revision":18821,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:47:35Z","sha256":"955254afb842728d10baf38e8f784e13d53d20b1e73476f6d5644586e5bc90f3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18821","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=T-65XJ3%20X-Wing%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-8dccb6eaa7710597","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:bd53073ee6d4d9a0"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The T-65XJ3 was developed as an offshoot of the T-65XJ during the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yuuzhan Vong"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong","referenceId":"reference:93079e2f7d73d480"}," Invasion. The Starfighter's design implemented a number of technical changes that were designed to give it an edge against the bizarre technology used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Yuuzhan Vong Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Yuuzhan_Vong_Empire","referenceId":"reference:418e7b3078742a07"},". As such, it represents the pinnacle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," design, and it is a favorite of Jedi Starfighter pilots.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Compared to the earlier T-65XJ, the XJ3 incorporated increased shield capacity, backup shield generators, more efficient fire control, and improved maneuverability. The backup shield generators allow a pilot to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Recharge Shields"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Recharge_Shields","referenceId":"reference:d4549c92a68a5d8a"}," at twice the normal rate, increasing the current ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"}," by 10 points, up to the XJ3's normal maximum of 30.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Starfighter's weaponry has likewise been upgraded, including wing-mounted ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Laser_Cannons"}," and three ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proton Torpedo Launchers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proton_Torpedo_Launchers"}," armed with four ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proton Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proton_Torpedoes","referenceId":"reference:89c41c332c03f2dd"}," apiece. Further, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"}," are \"Stutter-Fire\" capable, allowing them to bypass the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dovin Basal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dovin_Basal"}," defenses used by Yuuzhan Vong ",{"tag":"a","children":["Living Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Living_Vehicles"},". A Yuuzhan Vong ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dovin Basals"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dovin_Basals"}," provide only half ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"}," when defending against Stutter-Fire lasers.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["T-65XJ3 X-Wing Starfighter Statistics (CL 11)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children"